---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A timeline grid puts one row per resource, such as a room, a person or a machine, against a horizontal time axis.
  Set <code>resources</code> to the rows, as <code>&#123; id, title, supportingText? &#125;</code>, and
  <code>events</code> to the calendar's event objects with a <code>resourceId</code>. An event whose
  <code>resourceId</code> matches no resource is not shown, and <code>end</code> is exclusive, as in
  <code>wc-calendar</code>. <code>resource-label</code> names the resource column.
</p>

<p>
  With <code>editable</code>, people drag an event to another time or another row, and drag its edges to resize it.
  Each drop fires the cancelable <code>event-change</code> with <code>&#123; event, start, end, resourceId, action
  &#125;</code>; unless you cancel it, the grid applies the change. To save it on the server first, cancel the event
  and apply it later with <code>applyTimelineGridChange(events, detail)</code>. With <code>addable</code>, dragging
  across empty time in a row, or clicking it, fires <code>event-add</code> with <code>&#123; start, end, allDay,
  resourceId &#125;</code>. The range stays marked as a new event until <code>events</code> changes, or until you call
  <code>clearPlaceholder()</code>. Give an event <code>editable: false</code> to keep it in place.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-timeline-grid
    id='rooms-grid'
    resource-label='Rooms'
    editable
    addable
    style='height: 420px; width: 100%'
  ></wc-timeline-grid>
  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      const $grid = document.getElementById('rooms-grid');

      const today = new Date();
      today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

      function at(days, hours, minutes) {
        const result = new Date(today);
        result.setDate(result.getDate() + days);
        result.setHours(hours, minutes || 0, 0, 0);
        return result;
      }

      $grid.resources = [
        { id: 'aspen', title: 'Aspen', supportingText: '8 seats' },
        { id: 'birch', title: 'Birch', supportingText: '4 seats' },
        { id: 'cedar', title: 'Cedar', supportingText: '12 seats, video' },
        { id: 'elm', title: 'Elm', supportingText: 'Phone booth' },
      ];

      let nextId = 1;
      $grid.events = [
        { id: nextId++, resourceId: 'aspen', title: 'Design review', start: at(0, 9), end: at(0, 10, 30), color: 'red' },
        { id: nextId++, resourceId: 'aspen', title: 'Roadmap sync', start: at(0, 10), end: at(0, 11), color: 'blue' },
        { id: nextId++, resourceId: 'birch', title: 'Hiring panel', start: at(0, 14), end: at(0, 16), color: 'green' },
        { id: nextId++, resourceId: 'cedar', title: 'All hands', start: at(0, 11), end: at(0, 12, 30), color: 'blue' },
        { id: nextId++, resourceId: 'elm', title: 'Maintenance', start: at(0, 8), end: at(0, 9), color: 'orange', editable: false },
      ];

      // The grid applies moves and resizes itself; cancel the event to keep one.
      $grid.addEventListener('event-change', function(evt) {
        console.log('Changed:', evt.detail.action, evt.detail.event.title, evt.detail.resourceId, evt.detail.start, evt.detail.end);
      });

      // The grid only marks the range; adding the event keeps it.
      $grid.addEventListener('event-add', function(evt) {
        $grid.events = [...$grid.events, { id: nextId++, title: 'New booking', ...evt.detail }];
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
